WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.167
-Fox News and the
conservative movement

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.033
are still reeling from
the stunning revelations

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:06.667
contained in the most
recent court filing

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:09.501
from the $1.6 billion
Dominion lawsuit

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.467
which showed that in private,
Fox personalities

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.601
pushing the big lie
about the 2020 election

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.434
knew it was a lie,
and in some cases,

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:18.033
they even admitted that
they were disgusted by Trump

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.367
and that the entirety of his
presidency was a disaster.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.033
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:26.133
♪♪

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.934
It feels like Republicans
in Washington

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:30.501
and on Fox News can't go a day
without embarrassing themselves.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:31.834
They almost seem
to enjoy it,

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:34.067
like when they blew their chance
to win back the Senate,

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.200
thanks in part to

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.868
vampire/werewolf enthusiast
Herschel Walker,

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.434
when they made Kevin McCarthy
sit through

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:41.934
a [bleep] "Groundhog Day" reboot
to become speaker,

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:43.200
or when Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.701
lost her mind
at the State of the Union

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.234
in a white fur collar,
like a lady

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:47.501
screaming at
a Little League game

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:51.834
despite the fact that
none of the kids are hers.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:53.601
"You got to catch that, Timmy!"

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:57.234
"That kid's name isn't Timmy.
Who is that lady?"

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:58.734
"I can hear you
whispering about me!

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.267
I don't need to have a kid
on the team to be here, Timmy!"

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:03.200
"Does she think
my name is Timmy?

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.601
What is...?"

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:05.868
Yesterday, for example,

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:07.634
Oklahoma Senator
Markwayne Mullin,

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.868
a multi-millionaire
who owns a plumbing business

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:12.167
as well as two first names,

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.000
got into a tense exchange

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.734
with the president
of the Teamsters Union

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:18.033
during a committee hearing
chaired by Bernie Sanders.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.000
The hearing was about
the growing influence of unions

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.434
and the importance
of allowing workers to organize

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.734
without any illicit
corporate union busting.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:26.601
And as you can see
from this clip,

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:28.234
I think it's safe
to say unions are done

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:31.400
taking crap from wealthy CEOs
and their patrons in Washington.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.834
-You talk about CEOs
that are making all this money.

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.434
And what do you make,
Mr. O'Brien?

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:39.100
What do you bring
for that salary?

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.367
-What do I bring?
-Yeah.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:44.901
What job have you committed
or have you started?

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:47.234
What job have you created?
One job.

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:51.367
Other than sucking the paycheck
out of somebody else

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.300
that you want to say
that you're trying to provide

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.968
because you're forcing them
to pay dues?

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.033
-No, we don't force anybody --

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.300
-Senator, you've asked
the question.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.501
-You're out of line.

00:01:58.501 --> 00:01:59.868
-No, don't tell me I'm --
-You are out of line.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:03.033
-Don't tell me I'm out of line.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.133
-You frame the statement
like a tough guy.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:05.434
-You need to shut your mouth.
-Yeah?

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:06.467
-Because you don't know
what you're talking about.

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:07.501
-You're going to tell me
to shut my mouth?

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.801
-Yes, I did.
-Hold it, hold it.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.767
-Tough guy,
I'm not afraid of physical --

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:11.901
-Hold it!

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.334
-Don't sit there
and tell me I'm out of line.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:16.100
-As far as my salary goes,
my salary,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.567
if you follow me around,
I walk --

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:18.767
I actually look
at this building.

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:20.634
I bet you I work more hours
than you do.

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:21.934
Twice as many hours.
-That's impossible.

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.300
-No, that is -- that's true.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.300
We hold greedy CEOs
like yourself accountable.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.434
-You're calling me
a greedy C.E.O.?

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:28.701
-Oh, yeah. You are.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:29.934
-You want to attack my salary?
I'll attack yours.

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.100
-Go ahead!
-What did you make?

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.767
What did you make
when you owned your company?

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:33.968
-When I made my company?

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.801
I kept my salary down
at about $50,000 a year,

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.400
because I invested
every penny into it.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.200
-Okay. Alright.
You mean you hid money?

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.133
-No, I didn't hide --
Oh, hold on a second.

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:47.400
He said that's out of line.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.667
-We're even. We're even.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:53.133
-We're not even close
to being even.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.200
-Oh.
-You think it's smart?

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.167
You think you're funny?

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.067
-No.
-You're not.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:57.067
-You think you're funny.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:58.200
-Listen...

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.701
Mark, Marky-Mark, Markwayne.
Mark Wayne Gacy.

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:02.968
I can't remember.
It's obvious...

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:04.901
It's obvious from your accent,
you're from out of town.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.300
So as a New Englander myself,
let me give you some advice.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.033
Don't ever say,
"Do you think you're funny?"

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:12.501
to a bald teamster
with a Boston accent.

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:15.734
That's usually when the needle
drops on a Dropkick Murphys song

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:19.234
and the montage starts,
if you get what I mean.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:20.834
And based on the face
he's making,

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:23.667
I believe
he does think he's funny.

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:25.667
I also think he's funny, because
I don't want trouble either.

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:27.934
Now, CEOs in
the millionaire class

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.567
are clearly terrified
of the possibility

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:30.934
that workers might
have more power

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:32.567
if they can organize
without interference,

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:34.367
and you can see the terror
on Mullin's face.

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:35.968
In fact, the best part to me

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:37.434
is when the
multi-millionaire senator,

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:41.434
whose net worth is reportedly
between $31 and $75 million,

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:43.834
says he took a $50,000 salary

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.968
and then is immediately told
he's hiding it.

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:47.934
It catches Mullin so off-guard,

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:50.734
he has to hear it twice
before he's offended.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:53.200
-You mean you hid money?
-No, I didn't hide --

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.400
Oh, hold on a second.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:58.834
-It's like watching Moe Szyslak

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:02.567
realize there's no one
at the bar named "Mike Rotch."

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:05.167
"Hey!"

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.501
Also, I love Bernie
getting in the middle

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:09.467
of that whole thing to
restore --

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.667
There's something very funny
about referee Bernie.

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.501
"Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:15.734
I'm gonna say the same thing
about this fight

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.400
that I say about the big banks.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.067
Break it up!"

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:23.267
That clip once again exposes
the right's BS about standing up

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:24.734
for the working class
is all just a lie,

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:27.667
just like the lies they told
over and over and over again

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:30.234
about the 2020 election,
which they knew were lies,

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:33.067
as we've discovered
from the nonstop avalanche

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:35.200
of embarrassing revelations
in the Dominion lawsuit

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.234
against Fox News.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:37.734
Take Fox host Tucker Carlson,

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.300
who we learned this week
said in private

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.434
not just that the stolen
election lies were insane

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.767
and that he hated
Trump passionately,

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:47.501
but that the entire
Trump presidency was a failure.

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.534
-Thanks to the
$1.6 billion defamation lawsuit

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:52.968
filed by Dominion Voting Systems
against Fox,

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:57.501
we now know what Tucker Carlson
really thinks about Donald Trump

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:59.868
and about
Donald Trump's presidency.

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:04.501
Tucker Carlson said this
about the Trump presidency --

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:23.067
-And look, I know he was never
going to say that on camera,

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:24.834
but it would have been so fun
to see Tucker

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.801
after the election
being honest on TV

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.801
like a shellshocked
basketball coach

00:05:28.801 --> 00:05:30.334
giving a post-game
press conference

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.100
after losing by 50 points.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.901
"Hey, what was the biggest issue
out there today, Coach?"

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:40.701
"Ohhh."

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:42.267
Uh, I guess I'd say

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:45.234
the biggest issue is we, uh...

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:46.567
[bleep] suck at basketball?"

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:49.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.701
So Tucker admitted in private
there was no upside to Trump.

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:52.901
Now you tell me.

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:54.801
I was still waiting for
Infrastructure Week.

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:57.334
What about all his promises,
like great jobs

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:59.133
or great health care
or a great big wall?

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:00.367
What about the free hats?

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:04.801
Oh, God, were the hats
not really free?

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:07.067
It's such a stunning admission
that undercuts the entire

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:09.300
premise of the Trump presidency
and the devil's bargain

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.667
the conservative movement
has made with him.

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:13.501
It exposes their entire project
as a sham and a fraud.

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:15.601
They debase themselves for
a guy they were

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.734
personally disgusted by,
and at the end of it,

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:19.234
they admitted
they had nothing to show for it.

00:06:19.234 --> 00:06:21.200
It was all a lie
and they all knew it,

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.701
and now it's all
coming out in public,

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:24.467
they were shilling for Trump,
but in private,

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:26.534
they were saying --
-You're out of line.

00:06:26.534 --> 00:06:28.834
-The latest example

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:30.734
of a GOP election denier
caught lying is

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:32.767
former Trump campaign attorney
Jenna Ellis.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:35.100
You might remember her from that
infamous press conference

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:38.467
where she stood next to
Sidney Powell and Rudy Giuliani

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:41.701
while he leaked hair dye
live on television.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.200
And look, I'm not saying
it's the worst thing

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.067
Jenna Ellis and
Sidney Powell did that day,

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:47.033
but how come
neither of them stepped in

00:06:47.033 --> 00:06:49.467
when their friend
started to melt?

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:52.501
At least grab a fan or
a bucket or something.

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:54.801
If that press conference
had gone on any longer,

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:58.133
Rudy would have ended
in a puddle on the floor.

00:06:58.133 --> 00:07:00.501
"Quick, someone pour me in a
soda can and take me

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:02.400
to my next press conference.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.601
Just not a Diet Coke!

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:04.968
I don't want the boss
to drink me."

00:07:04.968 --> 00:07:06.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:08.501
In fact, Ellis followed Rudy
around on his tour

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:10.400
of swing states where he claimed
the election was stolen,

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.100
including that time Trump
called in on speakerphone

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.067
and she held up that phone
to the mic so Trump

00:07:16.067 --> 00:07:17.501
could ramble incoherently.

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:19.934
-I'm in the Oval Office
right now

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:22.801
and it's very interesting
to see what's going on.

00:07:22.801 --> 00:07:25.834
And this was
an election that we won easily.

00:07:25.834 --> 00:07:27.267
We won it by a lot.

00:07:27.267 --> 00:07:29.834
Anybody watching television
the night of the election

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:31.467
was saying, "Wow."

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.934
I was called by
the biggest political people,

00:07:33.934 --> 00:07:36.567
"Congratulations, sir,
on a big win."

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:38.501
And all of a sudden,
ballots were dumped

00:07:38.501 --> 00:07:42.067
all over the place and a lot
of horrible things happened.

00:07:42.067 --> 00:07:43.801
Very weird things happened.

00:07:43.801 --> 00:07:45.934
But they're not weird
to professionals

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:48.033
and they're not weird
to Dominion

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:50.501
and other people
that operate machines,

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:52.400
and they're not weird
to the people

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.334
that handle the ballots where
they were flooding the market.

00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:56.767
People were getting
two and three

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:58.868
and four ballots in their home.

00:07:58.868 --> 00:08:01.334
People that were dead
were signing up for ballots.

00:08:01.334 --> 00:08:06.100
Not only were they coming in
and putting in a ballot,

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:09.367
but dead people
were requesting ballots.

00:08:09.367 --> 00:08:12.234
-Trump always talked like he was
trying to distract bank security

00:08:12.234 --> 00:08:15.067
while Danny Ocean
broke into the vault.

00:08:15.067 --> 00:08:17.234
-"And now, if I wanted to open
a checking account,

00:08:17.234 --> 00:08:19.234
would the fees be higher
than with the savings account?

00:08:19.234 --> 00:08:22.634
Come on. Come on, Danny.
We're running out of time."

00:08:24.901 --> 00:08:27.367
As you heard there,
one of Trump's deranged claims

00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:29.567
was that dead people
were requesting ballots

00:08:29.567 --> 00:08:31.300
and the hosts on Fox
were all watching

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.400
and taking their cues again,
even though they were

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.367
privately complaining
about how insane it was.

00:08:35.367 --> 00:08:37.067
For example, according to
"The New York Times,"

00:08:37.067 --> 00:08:38.367
about a week after the election,

00:08:38.367 --> 00:08:40.701
Tucker Carlson reportedly asked
his producers,

00:08:40.701 --> 00:08:43.367
"Do we have enough
dead people for tonight?"

00:08:43.367 --> 00:08:46.167
I will say, Tucker often has
the expression of a man

00:08:46.167 --> 00:08:49.601
who has just been told
by a child, "I see dead people."

00:08:49.601 --> 00:08:52.601
Watch.

00:08:52.601 --> 00:08:56.968
-I see dead people.

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:59.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.501 --> 00:09:06.200
-I like that.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.534
It was the first time I saw it
and I liked it.

00:09:09.534 --> 00:09:10.767
The only time the question,

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:12.501
"Do we have enough
dead people?" is legitimate

00:09:12.501 --> 00:09:14.234
is when you're casting extras
for "The Last of Us."

00:09:14.234 --> 00:09:17.133
"Do we have enough dead people
for the shoot tonight?"

00:09:17.133 --> 00:09:18.634
"Regular dead
or mushroom dead?"

00:09:18.634 --> 00:09:19.701
"Do you think
you're being funny?"

00:09:19.701 --> 00:09:22.801
"Alright, alright! Relax."

00:09:22.801 --> 00:09:24.300
According to the "Times,"
that night,

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:25.767
he trumpeted the evidence
borrowed

00:09:25.767 --> 00:09:27.267
from a Trump campaign
news release --

00:09:27.267 --> 00:09:29.801
four allegedly dead Georgians
had cast a ballot.

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:32.033
Within days, though, the
campaign's spoon fed examples

00:09:32.033 --> 00:09:33.234
began to fall apart.

00:09:33.234 --> 00:09:35.868
Three of the dead
Georgians were actually alive.

00:09:35.868 --> 00:09:38.334
In fact, Tucker had to admit
that he was wrong

00:09:38.334 --> 00:09:39.667
in a humiliating correction.

00:09:39.667 --> 00:09:41.901
In a statement, he said,
"As we reported last week,

00:09:41.901 --> 00:09:43.534
dead Americans voted
in this election.

00:09:43.534 --> 00:09:44.734
We shared a few examples.

00:09:44.734 --> 00:09:45.968
But on Friday, we began to learn

00:09:45.968 --> 00:09:48.534
some of the specific dead voters
reported to us

00:09:48.534 --> 00:09:50.100
as deceased are in fact alive."

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:52.868
Man, no one's ever seemed
so bummed to learn

00:09:52.868 --> 00:09:54.400
that someone
they thought was dead

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.801
is actually alive.

00:09:55.801 --> 00:09:57.133
He sounds like a guy

00:09:57.133 --> 00:09:58.934
who poisoned his wife
for insurance money

00:09:58.934 --> 00:10:00.534
and then ran into her
at the country club.

00:10:00.534 --> 00:10:02.133
"Oh, Deborah!

00:10:02.133 --> 00:10:03.501
You're here.

00:10:03.501 --> 00:10:06.567
Didn't Jeeves make you
your martini last night?

